### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@sensorId = 1
@roomId = 1

### Create reading with current server time
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sensorId": {{sensorId}},
  "value": 23.1
}

### Create reading with explicit measurement time
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sensorId": {{sensorId}},
  "value": 23.1,
  "measuredAt": "2026-08-10T20:00:00"
}

### Get current reading
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensors/{{sensorId}}/current-reading

### Get reading history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings?from=2026-08-19T20:00:00&to=2026-08-20T20:00:00&limit=1000

### Get reading history with the default period (last 24 hours) and limit (1000)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings

### Export one sensor in long CSV format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings/export?roomId={{roomId}}&sensorId={{sensorId}}&from=2026-08-24T00:00:00&to=2026-08-25T00:00:00

### Export every sensor in a room in long CSV format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings/export?roomId={{roomId}}&from=2026-08-24T00:00:00&to=2026-08-25T00:00:00

# Both timestamps are required. Defaults limit an export to 30 days and 250,000
# rows. The CSV contains measured_at, received_at, room and sensor identity,
# sensor_type, value, unit, safe_min, safe_max, and status.

### Validation error: missing value
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sensorId": {{sensorId}}
}

### Not found error
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sensors/999999/readings

### Conflict error when the sensor, its room, or its lab is inactive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sensor-readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sensorId": {{sensorId}},
  "value": 21.0
}
